block newscontent
  p.card-text
  p Two contributions were accepted for the International Conference CyberWorlds 2021:
  ul
    li
      em
        strong
          a.external(href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.13787" target="_blank") Interactive Multi-level Stroke Control for Neural Style Transfer
      br
      | Max Reimann, Benito Buchheim, Amir Semmo, Jürgen Döllner and Matthias Trapp
    li
      em
        strong
          a.external(href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.05962" target="_blank") COLiER: Collaborative Editing of Raster Images
      br
      | Ulrike Bath, Sumit Shekhar, Jürgen Döllner and Matthias Trapp
  p
    | The conference is taking place 28.–30. September: 
    a(href="https://cyberworlds2021.sciencesconf.org" target="_blank") https://cyberworlds2021.sciencesconf.org
    | . This research was enabled by the collaboration of Digital Masterpieces and the Computer Graphics Systems Group (funded by the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF) through grant 01IS18092/"mdViPro" and 01IS19006/"KI-LAB-ITSE").
